e separate rules for the submission, review, and publication process for all MLPerf benchmarks 【123†here】.\nL249: The MLPerf name and logo are trademarks. In order to refer to a result using the MLPerf name, the result must conform to the letter and spirit of the rules specified in this document. The MLPerf organization reserves the right to solely determine if a use of its name or logo is acceptable.\nL250: ### 1.1. Definitions (read this section carefully)\nL251: \nL252: The following definitions are used throughout this document:\nL253: \nL254: A sample is the unit on which inference is run. E.g., an image, or a sentence.\nL255: \n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nExecution Providers | onnxruntime (https://onnxruntime.ai/docs/execution-providers/)\nciteturn80view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://onnxruntime.ai/docs/execution-providers/\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 266\nL0: 【0†Skip to main content】\nL1:   * 【1†ONNX Runtime】\nL2:   * 【2†Install ONNX Runtime】\nL3:   * 【3†Get Started】\nL4:     * 【4†Python】\nL5:     * 【5†C++】\nL6:     * 【6†C】\nL7:     * 【7†C#】\nL8:     * 【8†Java】\nL9:     * 【9†JavaScript】\nL10:       * 【10†Web】\nL11:       * 【11†Node.js binding】\nL12:       * 【12†React Native】\nL13:     * 【13†Objective-C】\nL14:     * 【14†Julia, Ruby and Rust APIs】\nL15:     * 【15†Windows】\nL16:     * 【16†Mobile】\nL17:     * 【17†On-Device Training】\nL18:     * 【18†Large Model Training】\nL19:   * 【19†Tutorials】\nL20:     * 【20†API Basics】\nL21:     * 【21†Accelerate PyTorch】\nL22:       * 【22†PyTorch Inference】\nL23:       * 【23†Inference on multiple targets】\nL24:       * 【24†Accelerate PyTorch Training】\nL25:     * 【25†Accelerate TensorFlow】\nL26:     * 【26†Accelerate Hugging Face】\nL27:     * 【27†Deploy on AzureML】\nL28:     * 【28†Deploy on mobile】\nL29:       * 【29†Object detection and pose estimation with YOLOv8】\nL30:       * 【30†Mobile image recogniti