\nL185:     `import onnxruntime as rt\nL186: \nL187:     sess_options = rt.SessionOptions()\nL188:     sess_options.enable_profiling = True\nL189:     `\nL190: If you are using the onnxruntime_perf_test.exe tool, you can add `-p [profile_file]` to enable performance profiling.\nL191: \nL192: In both cases, you will get a JSON file which contains the detailed performance data (threading, latency of each operator, etc). This file is a standard performance tracing file, and to view it in a user-friendly way, you can open it by using multiple tools.\nL193:   * (Windows) Use the WPA GUI to open the trace using the Perfetto OSS plugin - 【168†Microsoft-Performance-Tools-Linux-Android†github.com】\nL194:   * 【169†Perfetto UI†www.ui.perfetto.dev】 - Successor to Chrome Tracing UI\nL195:   * chrome://tracing:\nL196:     * Open a Chromium based browser such as Edge or Chrome\nL197:     * Type chrome://tracing in the address bar\nL198:     * Load the generated JSON file\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nInternal Error ()\nciteturn80view3 [wordlim: 200] Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://github.com/mlcommons/inference/tree/master/loadgen\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 1\nL0: Failed to fetch https://github.com/mlcommons/inference/tree/master/loadgen: Failed to fetch restricted URL\n"
